{"title":"1969 Canadian MO Problems/Problem 1","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1969_Canadian_MO_Problems/Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Show that if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/2/f/82f5bc2774e22b7f07c42968630ef24353324b73.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_1/b_1=a_2/b_2=a_3/b_3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"171\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/2/5/925a535dbb4b75e53997bf85ecca733334c669e4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p_1,p_2,p_3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"65\" height=\"11\" /> are not all zero, then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/3/1/9316912cf5e8837addac8f9654887bc8cc9255e2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\left(\\frac{a_1}{b_1} \\right)^n=\\frac{p_1a_1^n+p_2a_2^n+p_3a_3^n}{p_1b_1^n+p_2b_2^n+p_3b_3^n}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"233\" height=\"44\" /> for every positive integer <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/d/9/bd923e41635af40a1abe58f230732f2280b0723a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"10\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1969_Canadian_MO_Problems/Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Instead of proving the two expressions equal, we prove that their difference equals zero.\n</p><p>Subtracting the LHS from the RHS,\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/f/9/cf970c7956a3efc20f125225427ad3730e988dca.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0=\\frac{p_1a_1^n+p_2a_2^n+p_3a_3^n}{p_1b_1^n+p_2b_2^n+p_3b_3^n}-\\frac{a_1^n}{b_1^n}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -16px\" width=\"236\" height=\"40\" />\n</p><p>Finding a common denominator, the numerator becomes\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/2/4/324e508536241a0939f703341081f03d338535d7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b_1^n(p_1a_1^n+p_2a_2^n+p_3a_3^n)-a_1^n(p_1b_1^n+p_2b_2^n+p_3b_3^n)=p_2(a_2^nb_1^n-a_1^nb_2^n)+p_3(a_3^nb_1^n-a_1^nb_3^n)=0.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"712\" height=\"18\" />\n(The denominator is irrelevant since it never equals zero)\n</p><p>From <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/e/f/2efd414cc1145e9323c0480ebb2e68b11199c974.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_1/b_1=a_2/b_2,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"111\" height=\"18\" /> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/e/4/de411fb670b0b5ae5bcfbf32255c2f60f4072afc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_1^nb_2^n=a_2^nb_1^n.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"98\" height=\"17\" /> Similarly, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/c/5/0c54934ca66a286b6b4e1254e7d68fc5d5a86cc6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_1^nb_3^n=a_3^nb_1^n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"94\" height=\"17\" /> from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/b/e/1be72ad0d71d2741a98f43437869d7dabbd37399.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_1/b_1=a_3/b_3.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"110\" height=\"18\" /> \n</p><p>Hence, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/b/c/0bcd254645b9bec4091674a857a7ff41f844fad6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_2^nb_1^n-a_1^nb_2^n=a_3^nb_1^n-a_1^nb_3^n=0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"243\" height=\"17\" /> and our proof is complete.\n</p>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"clear:both; margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1969_Canadian_MO\" title=\"1969 Canadian MO\">1969 Canadian MO</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1969_Canadian_MO_Problems\" title=\"1969 Canadian MO Problems\">Problems</a></b>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"33%\" align=\"center\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b>First question</b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"34%\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1969_Canadian_MO_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"1969 Canadian MO Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1969_Canadian_MO_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"1969 Canadian MO Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1969_Canadian_MO_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"1969 Canadian MO Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1969_Canadian_MO_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"1969 Canadian MO Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1969_Canadian_MO_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"1969 Canadian MO Problems/Problem 6\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1969_Canadian_MO_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"1969 Canadian MO Problems/Problem 7\">7</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1969_Canadian_MO_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"1969 Canadian MO Problems/Problem 8\">8</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1969_Canadian_MO_Problems/Problem_9\" title=\"1969 Canadian MO Problems/Problem 9\">9</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1969_Canadian_MO_Problems/Problem_10\" title=\"1969 Canadian MO Problems/Problem 10\">10</a>\n</td>\n<td width=\"33%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1969_Canadian_MO_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"1969 Canadian MO Problems/Problem 2\">Problem 2</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<p><br />\n</p>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017170032\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: []\nCPU time usage: 0.020 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.045 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 74/1000000\nPost‐expa